ous one-off variant FindService returns a container of handles (see Chapter 5.3.3) for the matching service instances, which might also be empty, if no matching service instance is currently available. Opposed to that, the StartFindService returns a FindServiceHandle , which can be used to stop the ongoing background activity of monitoring service instance availability via call to StopFindService . The first (and specific for this variant) parameter to StartFindService is a user provided handler function with the following signature:"}],"v":1}
